Chapter 3

3. Discussions

3.1 Introduction

This chapter discusses how the Tic-Tac-Toe game will be designed and developed using Java.
It explains the design approach, the tools that will be used and how the different features of the game are expected to work.
It also discusses the programming concepts that will be applied during development.

3.2 Design Approach

The project uses an object-oriented programming approach.
This means that the program is divided into classes, where each class is responsible for a specific part of the game.
This helps to make the program easier to understand, organise and maintain.

The game is designed as a desktop application with a simple interface that allows users to play without difficulty.
The customary 3*3 Tic-Tac-Toe board is used, with X and O representing the two players.

3.3 Graphical User Interface

The graphical user interface (GUI) uses Java Swing to make the game simple and easy to use.
The application displays a customary 3*3 Tic-Tac-Toe board where players place their symbols, X and O.
It provides two game modes: Two-Player Mode and AI Mode.
In AI mode, users can also select the computer's difficulty level.

The interface includes a csoreboard that tracks the scores of X, O and ties. 
It also displays the game status and provides a New Game button and a Reset Score button to help users manage their games.

